# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PreflightQC .gitignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Third-party corresponding source (gate G-5) ---------------------------
# The FFmpeg source archive and the build-recipe archive are NOT committed: they are
# ~17 MB of upstream code, and Git is the wrong container for it. What IS committed is
# everything needed to rebuild them byte-for-byte — upstream repository, commit, archive
# prefix, exact command and expected SHA-256, all in packaging/binaries.lock.json.
#   python tools/fetch_corresponding_source.py
# The working checkouts those archives are built from are pure scratch space.
third-party/source/

# --- Third-party binaries -------------------------------------------------
# ffprobe, the libav* shared libraries and MediaInfo are NEVER committed to
# this repository. They are fetched at packaging time from their pinned,
# checksum-verified official sources and recorded in the dependency manifest.
# See docs/licensing/LICENSING-GATE-V1.md.
third-party/bin/
third-party/**/*.exe
third-party/**/*.dll
third-party/**/*.dylib
third-party/**/*.so
third-party/**/*.zip
third-party/**/*.7z
third-party/**/*.tar.xz
third-party/**/*.tar.gz

# --- Generated / synthetic test media -------------------------------------
# The golden corpus is GENERATED from a committed manifest, never committed.
test-assets/generated/
# Phase 1 spike media and raw inspector dumps: generated from a real encoder, large,
# and reproducible. The findings summary is small enough to keep; the raw matrix is not.
spikes/samples/
spikes/probe-matrix.json
test-assets/**/*.mp4
test-assets/**/*.mov
test-assets/**/*.mkv
test-assets/**/*.webm
test-assets/**/*.avi
test-assets/**/*.wmv
test-assets/**/*.m4v
test-assets/**/*.3gp

# --- Build / packaging output ---------------------------------------------
build/
dist/
out/
*.spec.bak
packaging/output/
packaging/staging/

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.eggs/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- Node (only if a reporting toolchain requires it) ---------------------
node_modules/

# --- Editors / OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store

# --- Local runtime state --------------------------------------------------
# Local custom client profiles and app config are user data, never committed.
*.local.json
local-profiles/
logs/
*.log

# --- Windows shell artefact -----------------------------------------------
# A literal, unexpanded "%SystemDrive%" folder that Windows itself occasionally
# creates in a working directory during heavy file activity. It holds Windows shell
# caches and is not produced by PreflightQC — nothing in this codebase references
# that variable. Excluded so it cannot be committed by accident.
%SystemDrive%/

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pfx
*.p12
*.snk
